.TH TRACE\-COLLECTOR\-GO 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded 158367ea" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
trace\-collector\-go \- Collect BPF trace events from the Kingdom's ring buffers and publish them to Wotan.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trace\-collector\-go
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Collect BPF trace events from the Kingdom's ring buffers and publish them to Wotan.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-untrusted\-ebpf\-obj\-dir
Development only: as root, load BPF objects from paths a non\-root user can write (e.g. a user\-owned ebpf/target). Off, such objects are refused
.TP
.B \-\-batch\-size \fIN\fR
Publish batch size (default 100)
.TP
.B \-\-batch\-timeout \fIDURATION\fR
Publish batch timeout (default 50ms)
.TP
.B \-\-buf\-size \fIN\fR
Event channel buffer size (default 8192)
.TP
.B \-\-ebpf\-obj\-dir \fISTRING\fR
Directory containing compiled BPF ELF objects (default: ebpf/target/bpfel\-unknown\-none/release)
.TP
.B \-\-enable\-flow\-tracker
Enable flow_tracker TC program (default true)
.TP
.B \-\-enable\-latency\-probe
Enable latency_probe tracepoint program (default true)
.TP
.B \-\-enable\-packet\-marker
Enable packet_marker XDP program (default true)
.TP
.B \-\-http\-addr \fISTRING\fR
HTTP listen addresses for health/metrics, comma\-separated; off loopback needs AUTH_ENABLED=true (default 127.0.0.1:16670)
.TP
.B \-\-interface \fISTRING\fR
Network interface to attach BPF programs (default lo)
.TP
.B \-\-log\-json
Use JSON log format
.TP
.B \-\-map\-pin\-path \fISTRING\fR
BPF map pin path (default /sys/fs/bpf/unheaded/)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-rate \fIN\fR
Max events/sec (0 = unlimited) (default 10000)
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-addr \fISTRING\fR
HTTP listen addresses (unified mode), comma\-separated; off loopback needs AUTH_ENABLED=true (default 127.0.0.1:16671)
.TP
.B \-\-read\-interval \fIDURATION\fR
Map read interval (default 100ms)
.TP
.B \-\-ring\-path \fISTRING\fR
BPF ring buffer pin path (default /sys/fs/bpf/unheaded/anamnesis_events)
.TP
.B \-\-unified
Run in unified mode (load all BPF programs)
.TP
.B \-\-wotan\-addr \fISTRING\fR
Wotan gRPC address (default localhost:18001)
.TP
.B \-\-wotan\-http\-addr \fISTRING\fR
Wotan HTTP address (fallback) (default localhost:18000)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
trace\-collector\-go
trace\-collector\-go \-\-interface eth0 \-\-wotan\-addr localhost:18001
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
